<v Zoe Chace>Fun is not the word, but I'm looking for something to happen, and it was happening.
<v Zoe Chace>好玩不是那个词，但我一直在期待发生点什么，而它确实发生了。

00:37:40.950 --> 00:37:46.410
<v Karlyn Borysenko>Yeah, it's an adrenaline rush. It's like this isn't-- this doesn't happen every day, right?
<v Karlyn Borysenko>是的，这是一种肾上腺素冲动。这就像——这不是每天都会发生的，对吧？

00:37:46.410 --> 00:37:50.510
<v Suzanne Gaber>Yeah. But it does seem like you guys are making it happen every day.
<v Suzanne Gaber>是的。但看起来你们这些人每天都在让它发生。

00:37:50.510 --> 00:37:51.610
<v Zoe Chace>Actually, it does happen every day.
<v Zoe Chace>其实，它每天都会发生。

00:37:51.610 --> 00:37:54.670
<v Suzanne Gaber>It seems like people are making it happen every day.
<v Suzanne Gaber>看起来是人们每天都在让它发生。

00:37:54.670 --> 00:37:55.770
<v Karlyn Borysenko>Oh, yeah.
<v Karlyn Borysenko>哦，是的。

00:37:55.770 --> 00:38:02.030
<v Zoe Chace>I give my business card to the guy who's famous for dressing as a frog at these protests. He was acting as a bouncer.
<v Zoe Chace>我把我的一张名片给了那个在抗议活动中以装扮成青蛙而出名的家伙。他当时充当保镖。

00:38:02.030 --> 00:38:03.900
<v Zoe Chace>Can you just give this to him?
<v Zoe Chace>你能帮我给他吗？

00:38:03.900 --> 00:38:10.700
<v Ira Glass>The scene at Chandler's ends with a bunch of streamers taking group photos of themselves simultaneously with their phones.
<v Ira Glass>在钱德勒家的场景以一群直播者同时用手机给自己拍合影结束。

00:38:10.700 --> 00:38:13.440
<v Chad Caton>Good job, boys and girls. You are all good kids.
<v Chad Caton>干得好，男孩女孩们。你们都是好孩子。

